# Title: Potentially Suspicious Image Load of Offreg.dll
# Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2026-07-23
# Level: medium
# Description: Detects potentially suspicious loading of the Offline Registry Library (offreg.dll).
# Offreg.dll enables direct read/write access to offline registry hives without invoking the Windows Registry API,
# bypassing its associated audit logging and telemetry. Attackers may abuse this to stealthily modify registry hives
# while evading detection mechanisms that rely on standard registry event logs.
# MITRE Tactic: Persistence
# Tags: attack.defense-impairment, attack.persistence, attack.t1112
# Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/image_load/image_load_susp_offreg_dll_load.yml
# False Positives:
#   - Third-party backup or forensic software that performs offline registry parsing
#   - Windows deployment tools (DISM, ADK) run from non-standard paths

ImageLoaded="*\\offreg.dll" NOT ((Image="*\\AppData\\Local\\Programs\\*" Image="C:\\Users\\*") OR (Image="*\\MsMpEng.exe" Image="C:\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Windows Defender\\Platform\\*") OR Image IN ("C:\\Program Files\\*", "C:\\Program Files (x86)\\*") OR Image IN ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\*", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*", "C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\*"))